1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
A win rate is a claim, not a record.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Anyone can post ninety percent and quietly delete the losses.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
And for an analyst who sells picks, there is no proof

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
they called it before the result — only their word, after the fact.

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Saksi turns the pick into a record.

6
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Seal it before the event: the selection is hashed,
and only the hash goes to Walrus Memory.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
Reveal it after: the server re-hashes the payload
and refuses if one byte moved.

8
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:41,000
Resolve it against a provider the analyst does not control.

9
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:46,000
Then memory argues back —

10
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:52,000
a recalled bias pattern can downgrade the next verdict.

11
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:57,000
This page has no session, no login and no database.

12
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:01,000
It reads Walrus Memory directly.

13
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Fifteen journals, sixty-nine memories, all from the relayer.

14
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:11,000
Here is the seeded demo journal — labelled synthetic, because it is.

15
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Twenty-four memories, seven picks, seven resolved, one bias pattern.

16
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Every row is the stored text itself.

17
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:27,000
A commit before the event. A reveal after.
An outcome with a Brier score.

18
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:31,000
And a bias the system noticed on its own:

19
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:37,000
two of two underdog picks above odds two-point-five lost.

20
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:41,000
Nobody typed that pattern in.

21
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Rebuild the journal from Walrus alone,
then compare it to the stored figures.

22
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Zero mismatches across three journals.

23
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Three services, one loop.

24
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:03,000
Walrus Memory is the record, not a cache —
if the database were deleted, the journal still reconstructs.

25
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:09,000
Tatum verifies the chain: this mainnet settlement is real,
status success, ten thousand atomic USDC,

26
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:12,000
confirmed before the payload was released.

27
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:17,000
x402 means the buyer signs with their own wallet;
the server never holds a key.

28
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:22,000
And the limits are on the page:
the oracle covers one league and one market.

29
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:28,000
Everything else is labelled self-attested, not verified.

30
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:33,000
Next: widen the oracle to more leagues and markets,

31
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:38,000
and aggregate across journals so reputation travels with the record.

32
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:42,000
One hundred and eighty-five tests, all green.

33
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:47,000
The demo journal is public — open it now at saksi-psi.vercel.app.

34
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:52,000
No wallet needed to read a track record.
